{"slug":"HeightFog","name":"HeightFog","namespace":"Ara","kind":"struct","declaration":"<pre class=\"shiki ara\" style=\"background-color:var(--code-background);color:var(--code-fg)\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:var(--code-keyword)\">public</span><span style=\"color:var(--code-keyword)\"> struct</span><span style=\"color:var(--code-type)\"> HeightFog</span><span style=\"color:var(--code-fg)\"> : </span><span style=\"color:var(--code-type)\">IComponent</span><span style=\"color:var(--code-fg)\">&#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:var(--code-type)\">HeightFog</span><span style=\"color:var(--code-fg)\">></span></span></code></pre>","summary":"<p>Exponential height fog lit by the sun, the sky and local lights (volumetric shafts where shadows cut the beams). Density halves every <code>falloff × ln 2</code> metres above <code>baseHeight</code>. The first entity in ID order wins.</p>\n","typeParams":[],"members":[{"kind":"property","name":"TypeIndex","signature":"<pre class=\"shiki ara\" style=\"background-color:var(--code-background);color:var(--code-fg)\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:var(--code-keyword)\">public</span><span style=\"color:var(--code-keyword)\"> static</span><span style=\"color:var(--code-keyword)\"> uint</span><span style=\"color:var(--code-fg)\"> TypeIndex { get; }</span></span></code></pre>","summary":"<p>Stable engine component index.</p>\n","typeParams":[],"params":[]},{"kind":"field","name":"Density","signature":"<pre class=\"shiki ara\" style=\"background-color:var(--code-background);color:var(--code-fg)\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:var(--code-keyword)\">public</span><span style=\"color:var(--code-keyword)\"> float</span><span style=\"color:var(--code-fg)\"> Density;</span></span></code></pre>","summary":"<p>Extinction at <code>baseHeight</code>, per metre. 0.002 is a light haze (visibility ≈ 1.5 km), 0.02 a thick fog (≈ 150 m).</p>\n","remarks":"<p>Range: [0, 0.1]. Default: 0.002.</p>\n","typeParams":[],"params":[]},{"kind":"field","name":"BaseHeight","signature":"<pre class=\"shiki ara\" style=\"background-color:var(--code-background);color:var(--code-fg)\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:var(--code-keyword)\">public</span><span style=\"color:var(--code-keyword)\"> float</span><span style=\"color:var(--code-fg)\"> BaseHeight;</span></span></code></pre>","summary":"<p>World altitude where the fog has its full density.</p>\n","remarks":"<p>Unit: m. Default: 0.</p>\n","typeParams":[],"params":[]},{"kind":"field","name":"Falloff","signature":"<pre class=\"shiki ara\" style=\"background-color:var(--code-background);color:var(--code-fg)\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:var(--code-keyword)\">public</span><span style=\"color:var(--code-keyword)\"> float</span><span style=\"color:var(--code-fg)\"> Falloff;</span></span></code></pre>","summary":"<p>Scale height: density falls by a factor of e over this many metres of altitude.</p>\n","remarks":"<p>Unit: m. Range: [1, 10000]. Default: 60.</p>\n","typeParams":[],"params":[]},{"kind":"field","name":"Albedo","signature":"<pre class=\"shiki ara\" style=\"background-color:var(--code-background);color:var(--code-fg)\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:var(--code-keyword)\">public</span><span style=\"color:var(--code-type)\"> Color</span><span style=\"color:var(--code-fg)\"> Albedo;</span></span></code></pre>","summary":"<p>Scattering colour (single-scattering albedo, linear). Grey-white for water fog, warm for dust.</p>\n","remarks":"<p>Default: [0.9,0.9,0.9,1].</p>\n","typeParams":[],"params":[]},{"kind":"field","name":"Anisotropy","signature":"<pre class=\"shiki ara\" style=\"background-color:var(--code-background);color:var(--code-fg)\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:var(--code-keyword)\">public</span><span style=\"color:var(--code-keyword)\"> float</span><